course: dictionary
lesson: 4863
title: Words that hide more than they show
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have a simple meaning and a second meaning that makes you think. The context, meaning the sentences around the word, helps you find which meaning the writer wants. «An iceberg is a piece of ice that has broken off a glacier into the sea, and most of it lies under the water.» The sentence tells you what an iceberg is, so you can use it to check your own idea.
explain: Phrases can be harder. "The tip of the iceberg" does not mean the top of some ice. It means a small part of a much bigger problem that you cannot see yet. A writer might say, "The broken window was only the tip of the iceberg," to warn that more damage is hiding out of sight.
explain: Test your meaning by putting it into the sentence. «About nine tenths of an iceberg is hidden below the sea, which is why ships keep far away.» If you swap in "the part you can see," the sentence still makes sense. That tells you the word works the way you thought.
fact: An iceberg is a huge piece of floating ice.
fact: Icebergs break off a glacier or an ice sheet and then float in the sea.
fact: «Iceberg» is a noun, and «icebergs» is the plural.
fact: About nine tenths of an iceberg is under the water, because ice is a little less dense than seawater.
fact: The Titanic sank in 1912 after it hit an iceberg.
fact: "The tip of the iceberg" means a small part of a much bigger problem that you cannot yet see.
exercise: «An iceberg is a piece of ice that has broken off a glacier into the sea.» Where does an iceberg come from? | A river bank | A tree in a forest | A volcano | *A glacier or ice sheet
exercise: Tom says "the tip of the iceberg" means the pointy top of some ice. What does the phrase really mean? | A bright, cold colour | A very slippery floor | A type of lettuce | *A small part of a much bigger problem you cannot see yet
exercise: «Cartoons often put a polar bear and a penguin on the same iceberg.» Why is that a mistake? | Both live in the desert | Penguins cannot swim | *Polar bears live in the north and penguins live mostly in the south | Icebergs are only found in rivers
test: «About nine tenths of an iceberg is hidden below the sea.» How much of an iceberg is hidden under the water? | All of it, so you cannot see any | One tenth | Half | *Nine tenths
test: Which phrase means a small visible part of a bigger problem? | Iceberg lettuce | A glacier in the sea | Ice sheet on the hill | *The tip of the iceberg
exam: Which statement about an iceberg is true? | It is a rock on the sea floor | It is a kind of fish that swims in rivers | It only forms in deserts | *It is a huge piece of floating ice that has broken off a glacier
